{"title":"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath_(Problem_11-20)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CanadaMath (Problem 11-20)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the area of the region enclosed by the graph of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/4/864191ae88a08202ee04fd5d9d1ddd4b594b4e94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2=|x|+|y|?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/4/f94da8073549d81e04fef66f1a1f40dbf4e60d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\pi+\\sqrt{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\pi+2 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\pi+2\\sqrt{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 2\\pi+\\sqrt{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 2\\pi+2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"613\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the case when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/d/44df9cb6ce6f056c64c197a004b64fc4dd3a5aa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/5/e55b6810db781e7d0c3f70e981fae71bd68c2040.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/9/579c6d245f6bbc2bf41fcc62182d7d032c5e7ee0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2+y^2=x+y\\]\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/5/2e585b5d19dc88abd1cd8d083f79cf210658ac93.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x - \\frac{1}{2})^2+(y - \\frac{1}{2})^2=\\frac{1}{2}\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"37\" />\nNotice the circle intersects the axes at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/6457ca2dcd40dc21d9aa0db18c66bbac9af4d899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/754e946d1a160f767f0f61cbd9460401c2d1c17f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. Find the area of this circle in the first quadrant. The area is made of a semi-circle with radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/7/cc7c4b51e06b26289d792878cbf9efac28aac903.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" /> and a triangle:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a45b86b9a5f727c22135e8c436797d6b574c59df.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A = \\frac{\\pi}{4} +\\frac{1}{2}\\]\" width=\"86\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/1/77121b786ebf303837357aa5aab877da041db676.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]draw((0,-1.5)--(0,1.5),EndArrow);draw((-1.5,0)--(1.5,0),EndArrow);draw((0,1)--(1,0)--(0,-1)--(-1,0)--cycle,dotted);draw(arc((1/2,1/2),sqrt(2)/2,135, 315),dotted);for(int i=0;i&lt;4;++i){draw(rotate(i*90,(0,0))*arc((1/2,1/2),sqrt(2)/2,-45,135)); dot(rotate(i*90,(0,0))*(1/2,1/2));}[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>Because of symmetry, the area is the same in all four quadrants. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/4/ff46cec0a025fed22b794987d9a3e00bcc1e834a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\pi + 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"88\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath_.28Problem_11-20.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath_(Problem_11-20)\">Video Solution by CanadaMath (Problem 11-20)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by CanadaMath (Problem 11-20)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Fast Forward to 33:32 for problem 18\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4osvFatUv1o\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4osvFatUv1o</a>\n</p><p>~THEMATHCANADIAN\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B\">2016 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> 